{
  "extends": ["//"],
  "tasks": {
    "test": {
      // @brainstrike/db tests are env-sensitive serialized PGlite lanes; never
      // let them replay from cache.
      //
      // WHEN TO ADD A `cache: false` CARVE-OUT (the invariant this file anchors):
      // the root `test` task caches with `outputs: []`, so a cache HIT replays a
      // previously-logged green WITHOUT executing the tests. That is only safe if
      // the lane's pass/fail is a pure function of the inputs turbo hashes
      // (source + pnpm-lock + tsconfig/biome/turbo config). Carve a package out
      // here (mirror this file) when its `test` lane's outcome can depend on an
      // input turbo does NOT hash. Two mechanisms seen in this repo:
      //   (1) NATIVE/EXTERNAL BINARIES whose result-affecting behavior is not in
      //       the source hash — a compiled node-gyp/N-API addon (its `.node` +
      //       host ABI), an installed CLI the test shells out to (git, node-pty,
      //       /bin/sh). If the binary is absent/wrong-ABI the lane FAILS, and the
      //       compiled artifact/ABI is invisible to turbo's file hash.
      //   (2) HEAVY WASM-PGlite LANES on wall-clock testTimeouts, whose pass/fail
      //       is sensitive to un-hashed CPU parallelism/contention (this file's
      //       own reason — see MEMORY: "db#test is flaky under turbo
      //       concurrency"). Caching also masks INTERMITTENT real failures: the
      //       first lucky green locks that source hash green forever.
      // A carve-out needs a NAMED mechanism, not a hunch; but on a REQUIRED check
      // genuine uncertainty resolves toward carving out (state the uncertainty in
      // the comment). Pure, deterministic logic/React-testing-library lanes stay
      // cacheable. Current carve-outs: db, agent, embeddings, file-import,
      // app-shell, web (PGlite); desktop, secure-fs-native (native binaries).
      "cache": false,
      // Strict environment mode filtering is INDEPENDENT of caching, so the
      // cache:false carve-out above does NOT exempt db's test task from having
      // CI/COVERAGE stripped. Redeclare passThroughEnv here explicitly: package
      // configs REPLACE (not merge) array fields, and the docs are silent on
      // whether an UNSPECIFIED array field inherits, so we do not rely on
      // inheriting the root's passThroughEnv. Keep this list in sync with the
      // root turbo.jsonc `test.passThroughEnv`.
      "passThroughEnv": ["CI", "COVERAGE"]
    }
  }
}
